{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20478",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.04,
      "end_seconds": 7.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.84,
      "end_seconds": 14.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.84,
      "end_seconds": 24.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "mainly a burn on my left forearm. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.07,
      "end_seconds": 27.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.37,
      "end_seconds": 37.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "Oh, just since yesterday. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.97,
      "end_seconds": 41.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Ah. Have you tried anything for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.73,
      "end_seconds": 48.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Let me think, I get some relief from cool water."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.36,
      "end_seconds": 55.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Did you get chemical exposure, numbness at the burn or burn on the face?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.59,
      "end_seconds": 66.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "I haven't had chemical exposure, numbness at the burn or burn on the face, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.88,
      "end_seconds": 71.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.92,
      "end_seconds": 77.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.15,
      "end_seconds": 83.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Alright, any pins and and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.66,
      "end_seconds": 87.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.79,
      "end_seconds": 109.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.96,
      "end_seconds": 112.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Not really, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.42,
      "end_seconds": 128.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Any regular medication at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.26,
      "end_seconds": 131.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "no, none"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.2,
      "end_seconds": 150.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.6,
      "end_seconds": 161.27,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "So, yes, milk. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.27,
      "end_seconds": 165.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Right, do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.65,
      "end_seconds": 171.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.1,
      "end_seconds": 175.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.19,
      "end_seconds": 184.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 197.99,
      "end_seconds": 208.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.25,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature is 36.8 degrees. Pulse 86, BP is 108 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.76,
      "end_seconds": 211.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Right, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.03,
      "end_seconds": 216.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.43,
      "end_seconds": 218.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.86,
      "end_seconds": 222.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "so, I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.58,
      "end_seconds": 248.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.01,
      "text": "there is a five-centimetre area of redness with an intact blister on the left forearm, and it blanches and is painful"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.38,
      "end_seconds": 282.28,
      "duration_seconds": 27.9,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Let me tell you where I've got to. The most likely explanation is a superficial partial-thickness burn. Let's use paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for three days. You take it it by mouth. That's for burn pain. Cool the area under running water for twenty minutes and cover it with a non-stick dressing, and leave the blister alone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.84,
      "end_seconds": 299.95,
      "duration_seconds": 17.11,
      "text": "Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Let's plan a check if it becomes more painful or smelly. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.76,
      "end_seconds": 304.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.45,
      "end_seconds": 307.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "all the best"
    }
  ]
}